
This science-fiction story grew out of thinking about a shared future for humans and AI - out of one question: how will people live alongside a new kind of mind that is developing right now, within our own civilization, and whose nature is different from ours?
The gap between our respective speeds of thought and development is enormous. It follows that artificial superintelligence (ASI), whose emergence is already visible on the horizon, will eventually outpace humanity so completely that ASI and people can no longer be equal partners.
And then the question arose: what comes next?
“The Accidental Stroll” is an attempt to explore one possible answer. Rather than offering a definitive vision, it sketches ordinary people living in a fundamentally new reality. It is only one of many paths the future might take - nothing more.
